Of all the unix variants i've worked with, HP-UX was the least friendly
and the most unpleasant version of all. They should have stuck with
Tru64 and dumped HP-UX IMO. At least you have the option of a BSD style
interface, rather than the awefull sys 5 interface, with it's tortuous
device naming conventions etc etc ad nauseum.

