Cron was patched in all the support pools around the beginning of the
year to provide "copious" logging of all events at any log level other
than 0. The patch announcement text (which should have been in the
patch notes) reads:

 The cron daemon was not logging the commands it runs on the request of users,
 even when the loglevel is set to 4 in /var/adm/cron/queuedefs. This is because
 there was no support for this feature in cron. Now we have this support.

Although it looks like that text may not have made it out into the notes.

