For those of you interested, I got this problem fixed...



One of the problems that I found out was that the vdump of the system
was made on another system, not sure why but this seemed to cause a
problem when I tried to use a different system to do the vrestore (even
though these 2 systems are identical HW & SW)...



This is the command that I used to do the interactive restore, which was
successful:





rsh wsx -n dd if=/dev/nrmt0a bs=64k | /sbin/vrestore -i -f - -o no


