>    executed code on the stack.

How do you address it? Or did it explicitly map the stack into both address
spaces (seems wasteful, given the page size).

Split I&D in V7 performed instruction fetches (and PC relative data fetches)
from a separate 64k address space than data access. If you branched to the
stack address in data space you would execute code from wherever that mapped
to in address space.

If RSX-11M didn't do that, then we're talking about a different concept than
what V7 did.

