> OK, I hadn't looked though all the 5.1B docs.  This gives us a good reason
> to move up to 5.1B.  We use OpenSSH and it prefers to use /dev/random.
>
> Thanks!
> Steven
>

Steven,

V5.1b also includes our version of ssh (from the ssh corporation with
some Tru64 specific coding) as part of the OS.  If you're running
a cluster our ssh is required for the cluster to work.  Also, since our
ssh is in a required subset, if you try to remove it and then later need
to install patches it could cause some problems with patch install.
So, it would be best when/if you upgrade to V5.1b that you try to use
our ssh instead of Openssh.  One thing that our ssh does not do is
support ssh v1.  If you need ssh v1 you can install Openssh in
addition to our ssh to handle the ssh v1 requests.  I'm including some
text that I received on how to set this up:

  They can still handle sshv1 requests.  To do that you would need to
  build and install openssh and then configure our ssh daemon to know
  the path to the openssh daemon.  The sshd2_config file options are:

        Ssh1Compatibility               yes
        Sshd1Path                       /usr/local/sbin/sshd
        Sshd1ConfigFile                 /usr/local/etc/ssh/sshd_config

Ann




