Erkki Aalto <aalto@cc.helsinki.fi> writes:

> I had simple mirrored LSM volume consisting of just two disks.
> It got messed up and now LSM won't start at all. The disks themselves
> seem to be intact and according to disklabel contain LSM stuff.
> I had not made a backup of the configuration. The data was backuped
> the previous  night, but some data is of course missing.
> Does anyone know a way to salvage data from an LSM volume?
> (I know perfectly well I screwed, please do not tell me that)

	After all dskx  had been got to their own place, the fix was
	to

voldctl enable           # this command was the key!
volrecover -s -b vol0    # this probably would have been run on next boot
mount xx#yy /yyy
All data was saved from perfectly working AdvFS domain.

	It seems, that when LSM has once figured it does not have any the disks
	needed, it will NOT automatically start even when all the disks are
	visible again.

	But one question remains: why did the OS changed dsk5 -> dsk7 and
	dsk6 -> dsk8 as an other disk was replaced on the same scsi channel?

	It shouldn't do that, now should it?
