I suspect this scenerio you have described is close to the reality of
these pyramid files.  The single pyramid file I posted about earlier is of
the type where its one resolution in one file.  The other types which we
use far more often are all resolutions combined into a single file. In
either case they are fragemented.

Wether or not the fragmentation of these files is directly affecting
performance I cant say. I will try to run some tests to get an idea. I do
know though that the general fragmentation listed by the system is
definitely affecting performance.  After running defrag users noticed a
significant increase in response times.

-Jason


